# oracle: pair amoeba on the AMOEBA water hexamer (non-periodic; data.water_hexamer.amoeba = w119amoeba_hexamer.data, amoeba_water.prm and amoeba_water.key as examples/amoeba, bond_style class2, angle_style amoeba, boundary s s s, one/five special bonds, cutoff 10): the buffered 14-7, permanent multipole and induced-dipole polarization terms, pe and every c_p term and the forces at step 0 and after 10 NVE steps (run 0, then run 10; the example runs 100 steps). No Ewald summation (the example has none). Six water molecules give several polarization groups.
# oracle-inputs: w119amoeba_hexamer.data w119amoeba_water.prm w119amoeba_water.key
# oracle-compare: thermo=all atoms=all rel=1e-8 abs=1e-10 skip=press,c_virial[1],c_virial[2],c_virial[3],c_virial[4],c_virial[5],c_virial[6]
# Measured with native LAMMPS (black box): the engine agrees with native in every thermo row (step 0 and step 10) to 1.5e-15 relative (c_p[5] at step 10) and the forces after 10 steps to 1.8e-13 absolute (atom 7 fy). press and c_virial are skipped for the shrink-wrapped box (volume ratio 1.00000012, see w119amoeba_polar).
units           real
boundary        s s s
atom_style      amoeba
bond_style      class2
angle_style     amoeba
dihedral_style  none
fix             amtype all property/atom i_amtype ghost yes
fix             extra all property/atom i_amgroup d_redID d_pval ghost yes
fix             extra2 all property/atom i_polaxe d2_xyzaxis 3
read_data       w119amoeba_hexamer.data fix amtype NULL "Tinker Types"
special_bonds   lj/coul 0.5 0.5 0.5 one/five yes
pair_style      amoeba
pair_coeff      * * w119amoeba_water.prm w119amoeba_water.key
compute         p all pair amoeba
compute         virial all pressure NULL virial
fix             1 all nve
thermo_style    custom step pe evdwl c_p[1] c_p[2] c_p[3] c_p[4] c_p[5] c_p[6] press c_virial[1] c_virial[2] c_virial[3] c_virial[4] c_virial[5] c_virial[6]
thermo_modify   format float %.15g
thermo          10
run             0
run             10
